{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Infra.Polylogarithm"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational.im_li3_zeta5_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational.im_li3_zeta5_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational.lean#L21-L31","doc":"**Proposition (`prop:bring-trilog-imaginary-tate-rational`,\narithmetic core).**\nTheorem A specialised at K = 5: `(K-1)(K-2)π³/(3K³)` at K=5\nreduces to `4·3·π³/(3·125) = 12 π³/375 = 4 π³/125`.  Per\nCopilot review: `field_simp` to clear denominators before\n`ring`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bring-trilog-imaginary-tate-rational","label":"prop:bring-trilog-imaginary-tate-rational","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/bring-trilog-imaginary-tate-rational.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational.imLi3Zeta5Value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational.imLi3Zeta5Value","kind":"def","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringTrilogImaginaryTateRational.lean#L18-L19","doc":"Tate-rational value at K = 5: `4 π³ / 125`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}